{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Standing over him.</b> To guard him." "<b>And the God of Yitzchak.</b> Even though we do not find in Scripture that the Holy One, blessed be He, dedicated His name over the righteous in their lifetimes to write 'the God of so-and-so,' because it is said ״הֵן בִּקְדֹשָׁו לֹא יַאֲמִין״ (Job 15) — here He dedicated His name over Yitzchak, because his eyes had dimmed and he was confined to the house, and he is like one dead, and the evil inclination had ceased from him — a comforting thought." "<b>Spread out beneath it.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, folded all the land of Israel under him, hinting to him that it would be easy for his sons to conquer — like four cubits, which is a person's place (Ḥullin, there)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :register {:flags {1 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:56.774286864Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}